ed theorem with the independent checker (kcheck.c)", "ucas": "check", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "name", "type": "name", "required": true, "description": "the theorem or library lemma"}]}, {"cmd": "axioms", "description": "the axioms of the proof library (definitions and the integer arithmetic of Z); with a name, the ones that theorem's proofs rest on", "ucas": "axioms", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "name", "type": "name", "required": false, "description": "a proved theorem"}]}, {"cmd": "lemmas", "description": "the proof library's lemmas and theorems", "ucas": "lemmas", "structured": true, "params": []}, {"cmd": "elliptic", "description": "an elliptic curve over Q: by default the summary (invariants, minimal model, Tate's algorithm: Kodaira symbols, c_p, conductor; torsion; rank bounds by 2-isogeny descent; generators and heights; periods, root number, L-values, analytic rank, BSD quotient), or one operation", "ucas": "ec", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "curve", "type": "string", "required": true, "description": "[a1, a2, a3, a4, a6], [a4, a6], or \"y^2 + x*y = x^3 - x + 1\""}, {"name": "op", "type": "enum", "required": false, "description": "what (default: the summary)", "values": "info|points|torsion|rank|local|minimal|analytic|periods|on|height|add|mul|order|wp|ap|model|integral"}, {"name": "args", "type": "string", "required": false, "description": "the op's arguments: a point \"(x, y)\" (on, height, order), two points (add), \"k (x, y)\" (mul), a height bound (points, rank), a bound on |x| (integral), a prime (ap), z as \"a+bi\" (wp), a model: short, montgomery, edwards, twisted_edwards, legendre"}]}, {"cmd": "diophantine", "description": "solve a Diophantine equation through an elliptic curve: a plane cubic (homogeneous in 3 variables, or affine in 2), a curve quadratic in one variable with a quartic discriminant, or z^2 = quartic(x, y); rational point, birational map to Weierstrass form (kept with its inverse), the group, combinations of generators mapped back, each solution substituted into the equation; with no solution, a proof where one is found (rank 0, or no rational point on the real component the conditions need)", "ucas": "diophantine", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "equation", "type": "string", "required": true, "description": "\"a/(b+c) + b/(a+c) + c/(a+b) = 4\""}, {"name": "positive", "type": "boolean", "required": false, "description": "every variable > 0"}, {"name": "integer", "type": "boolean", "required": false, "description": "integer values (affine equations)"}, {"name": "nonzero", "type": "boolean", "required": false, "description": "every variable != 0"}, {"name": "count", "type": "integer", "required": false, "description": "solutions wanted (default 1)"}, {"name": "maxmult", "type": "integer", "required": false, "description": "largest |coefficient| of a generator (default 30 for rank 1)"}, {"name": "search", "type": "integer", "required": false, "description": "point search bound"}]}, {"cmd": "weierstrass", "description": "the maps from a cubic or quartic curve to Weierstrass form, the minimal model and the group", "ucas": "weierstrass", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "equation", "type": "string", "required": true, "description": "\"x^3 + y^3 = 7*z^3\""}]}, {"cmd": "congruent", "description": "is n the area of a right triangle with rational sides: the curve y^2 = x^3 - n^2 x, its rank by descent, a triangle (checked) or a proof that none exists, Tunnell's counts", "ucas": "congruent", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "string", "required": true, "description": "a positive integer"}]}, {"cmd": "mordell", "description": "the Mordell curve y^2 = x^3 + k: the summary and its integral points up to a bound", "ucas": "mordell", "structured": true, "params": [{"name": "k", "type": "string", "required": true, "description": "a nonzero integer"}, {"name": "bound", "type": "integer", "required": false, "description": "|x| <= bound (defa