+{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"tools": [{"name": "analyze", "title": "Analyse a function", "description": "Exhaustive or sampled analysis of a function over its domain (machine types u8..u64, i8..i64, f16, f32, f64, real, int): values, range, where it is defined, wrapping and C UB, critical points, equivalence of two functions (with a counterexample), error and fit of an approximation, cost under a GPU cost model, the graphics fixed-function states (blending, logic ops, stencil) that compute a scatter's update, minimal gate networks (with a proof of minimality), cheaper equivalent implementations, polynomial/rational approximations.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- show(f*): the function, typed\n- table(f*, max): values at the points of the domain\n- parse(expr*): the expression fully parenthesised\n- range(f*, nocrit): min/max over the domain\n- domain(f*): the conditions of the partial operations and the inputs where F is defined\n- wrap(f*): nuw/nsw per operation, C UB, end-to-end agreement with the mathematical result\n- crit(f*): critical points, extrema, inflection points\n- equiv(f*, g*, ftz, nanbits): equal on F's domain? (with a counterexample)\n- fit(g*, f*, metric): choose G's extra parameters to approximate F\n- error(g*, f*): error of G as an approximation of F\n- cost(f*, model, consecutive): price under a cost model\n- rop(f*, model): graphics fixed-function states (blending, logic ops, stencil) that compute a per-cell update F(s, d), each proved and priced\n- gates(f*, basis, max, nodes, as_c): minimal gate network, with proof\n- find(f*, n, max): cheaper implementations under the cost model\n- more(n): the next results of the last find\n- approx(f*, in, options): polynomial/rational approximations, measured\n- approx_more(n): more candidates of the last approx\n- adamfit(f*, in, options): expression shapes fitted by Adam, ranked by 0.8 cost + 0.5 error (weights changeable), the best certified\n- dword(f*, tol, atol, ulp, model): f64 arithmetic over f32 (alone, or as double-word pairs) where the model prices that lower, with a derived error bound and its conditions\n- foldproof(f*, model): the float round trips the model's driver folds, and their rounding as integer arithmetic it cannot fold, proved equal\n- banks(accesses*, size, elem, model): the bank-conflict degree of shared-memory index expressions over a warp, and a proved index swizzle that lowers it when the model prices conflicts\n- intatomic(f*, count, tol, global, model): a float atomic add as an integer atomic add on fixed point, when its values are proved exact there (or within tol) and the model prices it lower\n- mma(shape, accumulator, tm, tn, tk, model, all, validate, nofile, seed): a warp's matrix product (PTX mma.sync m16n8k16 or m16n8k8, f16 A and B) on a GPU without a matrix unit: the dataflows priced under the model, the cheapest proved over the 32 lanes with its error bound, as GLSL\n- stoke(f*, steps, restarts, len, seed, model): MCMC (Metropolis-Hastings) over straight-line integer programs priced by the model; what reaches distance 0 is verified on the whole domain\n- pit(f*, g*, trials, seed): polynomial identity testing (Schwartz-Zippel): a probabilistic answer with its error bound\n- phash(f*, seed, model): a switch's keys hashed injectively into a table, when the model prices the lookup below the compare chain\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"show\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["show", "table", "parse", "range", "domain", "wrap", "crit", "equiv", "fit", "error", "cost", "rop", "gates", "find", "more", "approx", "approx_more", "adamfit", "dword", "foldproof", "banks", "intatomic", "mma", "stoke"