)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- ring(ring, modulus, what): a ring's structure (units, zero divisors, ideals ...), an element of it, or a value computed in it\n- inverse_mod(a*, ring, modulus): a multiplicative inverse (of a number, an element, a matrix)\n- order_mod(a*, ring, modulus): multiplicative order (of a residue, an element, a polynomial over GF)\n- phi(n*): Euler's totient\n- carmichael(n*): Carmichael's lambda\n- factorint(n*): integer factorisation (Pollard-Brent, Miller-Rabin)\n- legendre(a*, p*): the Legendre symbol (a/p)\n- jacobi(a*, n*): the Jacobi symbol (a/n)\n- sqrtmod(a*, ring, modulus): square roots mod n (Tonelli-Shanks, Hensel, CRT)\n- qr(n*): the quadratic residues mod n\n- primroot(a, n, ring, modulus): the smallest primitive root mod n, or whether a is one\n- dlog(a*, base, ring, modulus): the discrete logarithm\n- crt(congruences*): the Chinese remainder theorem\n- congruence(equation*, ring, modulus): a linear or polynomial congruence\n- magic(divisor*, type*): the multiply-shift for dividing by a constant\n- ring_factor(p*, ring, modulus): factor a polynomial over a finite field or Z/n (or an element of Z[i])\n- irreducible(p*, ring, modulus): Rabin's irreducibility test\n- primitive(p*, ring, modulus): is the polynomial primitive\n- ring_roots(p*, ring, modulus): roots of a polynomial in Z/n or GF(q)\n- ring_poly(p*, ring, modulus): a polynomial expression reduced over a ring\n- ring_gcd(p*, q*, ring, modulus): polynomial (or Gaussian integer) gcd over a ring\n- ring_norm(a*, ring, modulus): the norm of a quadratic integer\n- matrix(matrix*, op, rhs, ring, modulus): a matrix over Z/n or GF(q): its properties, det, rank, nullspace, inverse, or a solve\n- gf2matrix(f*, type*): a GF(2)-linear bit map as a matrix\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"ring\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema":