"string"}}}}}}, {"name": "x86", "title": "x86-64 costs and intrinsics", "description": "x86-64 cost models per µarch (Skylake, Skylake-X, Golden Cove, Raptor Lake, Zen 4, x86-64-v2/v3/v4; numbers typed from uops.info, Agner Fog and the vendor manuals, a few measured on this host, the rest estimates, each row tagged), a cycle-level throughput estimate of a function's x86 code (mca), and the intrinsics catalogue (SSE2 .. AVX-512, BMI, GFNI, AES, CLMUL) with exact lane semantics as ucas expressions, tested against the C compiler (x86check).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- x86_models(): the x86 µarch cost models (skl skx glc rpl zen4 x86v2 x86v3 x86v4)\n- x86_model(name*): one x86 µarch: features, ports, and per instruction class latency, reciprocal throughput, uops and ports at xmm/ymm/zmm (with where each number comes from)\n- mca(f*, model): a cycle-level throughput estimate of a function's x86 code (critical path, port pressure, front end; no caches or mispredictions)\n- intrinsic(name*, model): one x86 intrinsic: signature, features, instruction class, exact lane semantics (as ucas expressions) and costs per µarch\n- intrinsics(filter, model): the intrinsics catalogue: count per feature, or the names matching a filter (a substring, a feature such as avx2, or a class)\n- x86check(filter, n, avx512): test the intrinsics' lane semantics against the host C compiler's intrinsics (compiled and run on random and edge inputs)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"x86_models\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["x86_models", "x86_model", "mca", "intrinsic", "intrinsics", "x86check"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "abstract_algebra", "title": "Abstract algebra, exactly", "description": "Exact algebra with certificates: integers of any size (bigint), integer matrices (Smith and Hermite forms with unimodular transforms, kernels, images, solving over Z; rational matrices), finitely generated abelian groups (\"Z/4 + Z/6\", \"coker [[2, 0], [0, 3]]\"): invariants, isomorphisms with explicit maps, Hom, tensor, Tor, Ext, homomorphisms with kernel/image/cokernel, subgroups, element orders, exactness; permutation groups by Schreier-Sims (\"S4\", \"(1 2 3), (1 2)\": order, orbits, solvable, nilpotent, centre, membership, subgroups, cosets, homomorphisms) and Cayley tables; polynomial ideals over Q and F_p (Groebner bases with cofactors, membership certificates, ideal equality); modules over F[x] (Smith form, rational canonical form).  Every claim is checked (U A V = D, preimages, inverse maps) and the check is reported.  For instance {\"op\": \"abiso\", \"args\": {\"g\": \"Z/4 + Z/6\", \"h\": \"Z/2 + Z/12\"}} or {\"op\": \"snf\", \"args\": {\"matrix\": [[2, 4], [6, 8]]}}.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- bigint(expr*): an exact integer expression of any size (+ - * ^ !, / exact, div floor, % mod, gcd, lcm, abs, isprime, binomial)\n- bigint_factor(n*): prime factorization of an integer of any size (Pollard-Brent rho; product and primality checked)\n- snf(matrix*): Smith normal form U A V = D with U, V and their inverses, verified; the cokernel\n- hnf(matrix*): row Hermite normal form H = U A with U unimodular, verified\n- zmatrix(op, matrix*, rhs): an integer matrix over Z: summary, det, rank, kernel (saturated basis), image (lattice basis), inverse over Z, cokernel group, or solve A x = b over Z\n- qmatrix(op, matrix*, rhs): a matrix over Q (entries like \"1/2\"): rref, det, rank, inverse, nullspace, solve\n- abgroup(group*): a finitely generated abelian group: invariant factors, primary decomposition, order, rank, exponent, torsion, generators\n- abiso(g*, h*): are two abelian groups isomorphic; if so an explicit isomorphism and its inverse, both checked\n- abhom(g*, h*): the group Hom(G, H)\n- abtensor(g*, h*): the tensor product G (x) H\n- abtor(g*, h*): Tor(G, H) from a free resolution\n- abext(g*, h*): Ext(G, H) from a free resolution\n- abmap(from*, to*, matrix*): a homomorphism G -> H given by the images of G's generators (columns, in H's generators): well defined?, kernel, image, cokernel, injective, surjective, inverse\n- abelem(group*, element*): an element of an abelian group: canonical form and order\n- absub(group*, generators*): the subgroup generated by elements, its quotient and index (membership witnesses checked)\n- abexact(g1*, g2*, g3*, f*, g*): is G1 -f-> G2 -g-> G3 exact at G2 (with preimages of ker g as the certificate)\n- permgroup(group*): a permutation group by Schreier-Sims: order (exact, any size), base and strong generators, orbits, abelian, derived and lower central series, solvable, nilpotent, centre\n- permelem(group*, perm*): is a permutation in the group (sifting, with the word in the transversals as the certificate); its order\n- permsub(h*, g*): H in G: subgroup?, normal?, index, normal closure, coset representatives\n- permhom(from*, to*, images*): does sending G's generators to the given permutations define a homomorphism G -> H\n- cayley(table*): a finite group by its Cayley table (entries 0..n-1): the axioms checked, abelian, element orders, solvable, nilpotent\n- groebner(polys*, order, modulus, vars): the reduced Groebner basis of an ideal of polynomials over Q or F_p, each element with its cofactors in the generators (Buchberger with criteria; verified)\n- idealmember(h*, polys*, order, modulus, vars): is h in the ideal: the cofactors h = sum c_j f_j (multiplied out and checked), or the nonzero normal form\n- idealeq(i*, j*, order, modulus, vars): compare two ideals: equal, one inside the other, or neither (each inclusion certified by cofactors)\n- fxmodule(matrix*, modulus): F^n as an F[x]-module with x acting by a matrix: invariant factors, minimal and characteristic polynomial, rational canonical form (Smith form over F[x])\n- pmsnf(matrix*, modulus): the Smith normal form of a matrix of polynomials in one variable over Q or F_p, with U and V\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"bigint\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["bigint", "bigint_factor", "snf", "hnf", "zmatrix", "qmatrix", "abgroup", "abiso", "abhom", "abtensor", "abtor", "abext", "abmap", "abelem", "absub", "abexact", "permgroup", "permelem", "permsub", "permhom", "cayley", "groebner", "idealmember", "idealeq", "fxmodule", "pmsnf"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them