e": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "elliptic", "title": "Elliptic curves and Diophantine equations", "description": "Elliptic curves over Q, exactly (analytic values with error bounds): invariants, minimal models, Tate's algorithm, conductor, torsion, rank by 2-isogeny descent, generators, canonical heights, the group law, models (Montgomery, Edwards, Legendre) with their maps, periods, L-values, BSD; Diophantine equations reduced to elliptic curves (\"a/(b+c) + b/(a+c) + c/(a+b) = 4\" positive), congruent numbers, Mordell curves, sums of two cubes.  A curve is \"[a1, a2, a3, a4, a6]\", \"[a4, a6]\" or \"y^2 = x^3 - x\".  For instance {\"op\": \"diophantine\", \"args\": {\"equation\": \"a/(b+c) + b/(a+c) + c/(a+b) = 4\", \"positive\": true}}.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- elliptic(curve*, op, args): an elliptic curve over Q: by default the summary (invariants, minimal model, Tate's algorithm: Kodaira symbols, c_p, conductor; torsion; rank bounds by 2-isogeny descent; generators and heights; periods, root number, L-values, analytic rank, BSD quotient), or one operation\n- diophantine(equation*, positive, integer, nonzero, count, maxmult, search): solve a Diophantine equation through an elliptic curve: a plane cubic (homogeneous in 3 variables, or affine in 2), a curve quadratic in one variable with a quartic discriminant, or z^2 = quartic(x, y); rational point, birational map to Weierstrass form (kept with its inverse), the group, combinations of generators mapped back, each solution substituted into the equation; with no solution, a proof where one is found (rank 0, or no rational point on the real component the conditions need)\n- weierstrass(equation*): the maps from a cubic or quartic curve to Weierstrass form, the minimal model and the group\n- congruent(n*): is n the area of a right triangle with rational sides: the curve y^2 = x^3 - n^2 x, its rank by descent, a triangle (checked) or a proof that none exists, Tunnell's counts\n- mordell(k*, bound): the Mordell curve y^2 = x^3 + k: the summary and its integral points up to a bound\n- cubesum(k*, positive): k as a sum of two rational cubes: x^3 + y^3 = k z^3 solved through its curve\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"elliptic\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["elliptic", "diophantine", "weierstrass", "congruent", "mordell", "cubesum"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "elliptic_ff", "title": "Elliptic curves over finite fields and cryptography", "description": "Curves over F_p (any size to 521 bits; named: secp256k1, P-256, P-384, P-521, Curve25519, Ed25519, Curve448, BN254, BLS12-381) and GF(2^m): #E by naive/BSGS/CM/Schoof with a certificate, group structure, twists, embedding degrees, scalar multiplication, ECDSA (RFC 6979), ECDH, X25519/X448, Ed25519, SEC 1 encodings, test vectors; discrete logs (Pohlig-Hellman, rho, MOV, Smart); Weil/Tate pairings; CM and Hilbert class polynomials; modular polynomials, Velu isogenies, isogeny graphs, division polynomials; ECM factoring and ECPP certificates.  A curve is a name, \"y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 mod 97\" or \"[a, b] mod p\".  Mathematics, not hardened (constant-time) cryptography.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- ec_info(curve*): a curve over F_p: discriminant, j, #E (certified by point orders), trace, group structure (certified by a Weil pairing), twist, embedding degree, weaknesses\n- ec_order(curve*, method, timed): #E(F_p) by a chosen method, with the certificate (points whose orders leave one candidate in the Hasse interval)\n- ec_points(curve*): the points of E(F_p), p <= 100000\n- ec_add(curve*, P*, Q*): P + Q\n- ec_mul(curve*, k*, P*, method): k P by wNAF/Jacobian, checked against affine double-and-add, the Montgomery ladder and plain NAF\n- ecm(n*, B1, B2): factor an integer (up to 576 bits): trial division, Pollard rho, Lenstra ECM stage 1 + 2; with B1 one ECM run\n- ecdsa_sign(curve*, key*, hash, nonce, msg*): ECDSA signature with RFC 6979 deterministic nonce (variable-time code: mathematics, not a hardened implementation)\n- ecdsa_verify(curve*, pub*, r*, s*, hash, msg*): verify an ECDSA signature\n- ecdh(curve*, a*, b, pub): Diffie-Hellman on a named curve: both sides from two private keys, or one key and a peer's point (validated)\n- x25519(k*, u): RFC 7748 X25519 (hex, little-endian)\n- x448(k*, u): RFC 7748 X448 (hex, little-endian)\n- ed25519_sign(secret*, msghex*): RFC 8032 Ed25519 signature (and the public key)\n- ed25519_verify(pub*, sig*, msghex*): verify an Ed25519 signature\n- ec_compress(curve*, P*): SEC 1 encodings of a point\n- ec_decompress(curve*, hex*): decode a SEC 1 point\n- ec_validate(curve*, P*): public-key validation (SEC 1 3.2.2.1)\n- ec_vectors(): run the built-in RFC/FIPS test vectors and the named curves' parameter checks\n- ec_dlog(curve*, P*, Q, secret, method): a discrete logarithm k with k P = Q: Pohlig-Hellman, BSGS, rho, MOV (pairing transfer), Smart (anomalous); checked by k P = Q\n- ec_weak(kind*, bits*): generate a weak curve (anomalous: #E = p; supersingular: embedding degree 2); \"anomalous 64\" also works as the curve of ec_dlog\n- ec_pairing(curve*, P, Q, n, kind): Weil or reduced Tate pairing by Miller's algorithm with bilinearity checks; on bn254/bls12_381 alone: e(G1, G2) in F_p^12\n- hilbert(D*): the Hilbert class polynomial H_D (CM j-invariants), rounding error bounded\n- ec_cm(D*, p, bits): a CM curve with discriminant D over F_p, or a random prime-order CM curve of a given size\n- ecpp(n*): an Atkin-Morain ECPP primality certificate, verified by an independent checker\n- modpoly(l*, p): the classical modular polynomial Phi_l (over Z, or mod p)\n- ec_isogeny(curve*, kernel, l): an isogeny from a kernel point (Velu, Kohel, checked as a homomorphism), or the rational l-isogenies (roots of Phi_l)\n- ec_volcano(curve*, l*): the l-isogeny graph around j(E)\n- ec_divpoly(curve*, n*): the division polynomial psi_n, its roots and factor degrees (the torsion field)\n- ec_binary(curve*, mul): a binary curve y^2 + xy = x^3 + a x^2 + b over GF(2^m): count (Koblitz, naive), FIPS parameters checked\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"ec_info\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ec_info", "ec_order", "ec_points", "ec_add", "ec_mul", "ecm", "ecdsa_sign", "ecdsa_verify", "ecdh", "x25519", "x448", "ed25519_sign", "ed25519_verify", "ec_compress", "ec_decompress", "ec_validate", "ec_vectors", "ec_dlog", "ec_weak", "ec_pairing", "hilbert", "ec_cm", "ecpp", "modpoly", "ec_isogeny", "ec_volcano", "ec_divpoly", "ec_binary"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "objec